<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17005" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτελεύτ-ητος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not brought to an end</i>
			or <i>issue, unaccomplished,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτελευτήτῳ ἐπὶ ἔργῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					4.175
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1.527
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>without an end, interminable,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Parm.
				8.32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				204a5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cael.</u>
				273a5
			</span></i>; <i>everlasting,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ πᾶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ocell.
					1.2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.114f
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of a
			person, <i>impracticable,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄτεγκτος κἀτελεύτητος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					336
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
